      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 15, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1689\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school name and the highest average number of enrolled students per department (among its degree-granting departments, excluding Chemistry, and only considering subjects with at least one enrolled student), and for each subject offered by the Chemistry department in the 2019FA term that has course materials, what is the subject title, the dense rank of the subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students descending, the full name of the offering department, and the school name of the Chemistry department? List the school name and highest average enrolled students per department first, followed by the Chemistry subject title, dense rank, department full name, and Chemistry school name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3224\", \"desc\": \"List all subjects from the term \\\"2010FA\\\" and all subjects offered in the term with code \\\"2025FA\\\", showing for each row: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank of the subject within each academic year group ordered by subject ID, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the source term (\\\"2010FA\\\" or \\\"2025FA\\\"). The columns should appear in the following order: subject ID, term description, material status key, academic year, rank, subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term start date, term end date, term parameter, minimum enrolled students per department, and source term. Order the results by subject ID and source term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3727\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, or for each department that offered more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of tip materials. List the department code, department name, department full name, number of subjects offered, total number of enrolled students, and total number of tip materials in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4738\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", show the subject ID, subject title, offering department name, term description, and the rank of the subject within its offering department. For each tip detail record where the material status key is 'RQ', show the subject ID, term description, term start date, tip material key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the financial aid year. Additionally, for each subject offered in \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\", include the academic year description from the academic terms table. Indicate the source of each row as either 'SubjectOffered' or 'TipDetail'. The results should be ordered by subject ID and source. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3904\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3590\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3277\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4305\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2591\", \"desc\": \"For all subjects in the 2014FA term with at least one enrolled student, show the subject title, offering department name, responsible faculty name, the TIP material status key, the total number of units, and the minimum total number of units in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the course number, along with the cluster type description and the HGN code description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4287\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key equal to 'U' and for subjects offered in the term with code '2025FA', show the library course instructor key, library reserve catalog key, term code, subject ID, the tip material key, tip material status key, tip ISBN, the subject title from the subject offered table, the minimum tip material status key in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the number of enrolled students (only including those where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average across all subjects), the offering department name, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, the offering school name, and the responsible faculty name for each subject. Order the results by offering department and descending number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_451face51eb6442bafa43e53",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 15, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"name\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"name\": \"Subject Offering Fact Tables\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"name\": \"Term Code\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Subject Identifier\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"name\": \"Total Credit Units\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Master Subject Identifier\"}]}"
    },
