      "content": "The database connection has been persistently unavailable (authentication error `1045 (28000)` on every one of ~14 attempts), so I completed all verification through the semantic network. Below is the investigation report, followed by the final SQL.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors):**\n\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — Textbook Information Program detail; one row per subject-material-status per term. Key columns: `TIP_MATERIAL_KEY` (material identifier → the count measure), `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` ('RQ','EO','RC','PC','BR','CL','NM','U',… ), `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `RECORD_COUNT`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Term dimension; carries `IS_REGULAR_TERM` ('Y'/'N') — the *only* term table with this flag (ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL lacks it). Used to scope \"regular academic terms.\"\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY** — Subject-level summary per term; supplies `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`. Joins TIP_DETAIL via TERM_CODE + SUBJECT_ID.\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Library reserve scope subjects per term; supplies `SUBJECT_TITLE`, `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, `RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — Subject-level rollup; supplies `TOTAL_UNITS` and `COURSE_NUMBER` (the window ordering key). Joins via SUBJECT_ID.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — Department dimension; supplies `SCHOOL_NAME`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`. Joins on `DEPARTMENT_NAME`.\n- **SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT** — Administrative department; supplies `DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER`. Joins via `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`.\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS / ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** — investigated; not required (TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the parent of TIP_DETAIL but the question counts materials directly from TIP_DETAIL; TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS only decodes status text, not needed; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL lacks IS_REGULAR_TERM).\n\n**Concepts / column-concepts:** `concept_course_material_programs`, `concept_department_dimension`, `column_concept_total_units`, `column_concept_material_status_key`, `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_term_code`, `column_concept_department_name`, `column_concept_enrollment_measures` — all confirm the join semantics used below.\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- `ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ TIP_DETAIL.TERM_CODE` and `↔ SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE` (plus SUBJECT_ID to avoid fan-out, per precedent dw_3727).\n- `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID` (SUBJECT_ID-only joins, per precedent dw_2591 and the hint's join keys).\n- `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE`; SIS_DEPARTMENT joined on department name (per dw_4724).\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences & Fitness\n- **Term table**: ACADEMIC_TERMS (has IS_REGULAR_TERM) vs ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (lacks it) → \"regular academic terms\" **requires ACADEMIC_TERMS**.\n- **Total units source**: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS (hint-specified, pairs with COURSE_NUMBER for the window) vs SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS → use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY per hint and dw_2591.\n- **Department name**: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME (TopSubjects side) vs LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME (2014FA side) — both required, in separate union branches.\n- **Material count**: COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) per hint (not SUM(RECORD_COUNT)).\n\n## 4. Business Usage / Precedents\n- **dw_2591** is the exact precedent for the 2014FA branch (LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ TIP_DETAIL ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, `MIN(TOTAL_UNITS) OVER (ORDER BY COURSE_NUMBER ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING)`, filter TERM_CODE='2014FA' AND NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>0).\n- **dw_3727** is the precedent for the regular-term TIP material count (TIP_DETAIL ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS ⋈ SUBJECT_SUMMARY on TERM_CODE+SUBJECT_ID, IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y').\n- **dw_4724** is the precedent for attaching SCHOOL_NAME + DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER via SIS_DEPARTMENT (on dept name) → SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.\n- **dw_3224 / dw_3436 / dw_4738 / dw_3277 / dw_3590** establish the UNION-ALL-with-source-label pattern: fill relevant columns, NULL the rest, append the reason label.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated via `semantic_get` / `semantic_graph`: TIP_DETAIL, ACADEMIC_TERMS, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, and the relevant concepts/column-concepts. Database execution was **not possible** (persistent auth failure), so verification is semantic-network-based.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\nTwo-branch UNION ALL following the precedents: a `TopSubjects` CTE (top-10 subjects by COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) over regular terms) and a `Subjects2014FA` CTE (dw_2591 shape), each enriched with SCHOOL_NAME/DEPARTMENT_PHONE via SIS_DEPARTMENT→SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT, then unioned with NULLs for non-applicable columns and the reason label. SELECT list = exactly the 11 requested columns in order.\n\n",
